  "methodology": [
    "Four sequential samples on the same already-running authorized Cloud Shell environment, using start/addPublicKey/addPublicKey/start order.",
    "Each sample generates a fresh RSA-3072 key, makes one registration mutation, completes its operation, reads back RUNNING state and key registration, and executes SSH true.",
    "An operation not complete on response would be polled every 250ms; all four responses were already complete.",
    "Each ephemeral public key was removed with the provider API and confirmed absent; each temporary private-key directory was removed.",
    "Credentials were loaded only in server memory from the existing encrypted authorization. No application was launched, stopped, rebuilt or modified."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Two samples per method on one environment are a timing probe, not a statistically established performance guarantee.",
    "Key generation and the initial environment read are excluded from totalSetupMs; operation, confirming environment read and SSH are included.",
    "The comparison does not measure artifact delivery, product rendering, cold provisioning or full launch latency.",
    "No production change was made; addPublicKey remains an optimization candidate that would need deadline, uncertain-response, suspension-race and native acceptance coverage."
  ],
